  "chapter": {
    "number": 28,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(29) A Psalm of David on the occasion of the solemn assembly of the Tabernacle."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Bring to the Lord, you⌃ sons of God, bring to the Lord young rams; bring to the Lord glory and honor.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Bring to the Lord glory, due to his name; worship the lord in his holy court.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The voice of the Lord is upon the waters: the God of glory has thundered: the Lord is upon many waters.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The voice of the Lord is mighty; the voice of the Lord is full of majesty.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "There is the voice of the Lord who breaks the cedars; the Lord will break the cedars of Libanus.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he will beat them small, even Libanus itself, like a calf; and the beloved one is as a young unicorn.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "There is a voice of the Lord who divides a flame of fire.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "A voice of the Lord who shakes the wilderness; the Lord will shake the wilderness of Cades.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The voice of the Lord",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 52
          },
          {
            "text": "strengthens the hinds, and will uncover the thickets: and in his temple every one speaks of his glory.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord will dwell on the waterflood: and the Lord will sit a king for ever.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord will give strength to his people; the Lord will bless his people with peace.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 52,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. participle.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 28,
          "verse": 9
        }
      }
    ]
  },
